nd when  I see him look at me like you wrote that  dad it's a good feeling how do you you  know I always wonder for a lot of you  know musicians such as yourself or  people of notoriety who grew up in a  certain facet a certain way I always  wonder how do you instill that same  hunger and indifferent and maybe you  know the adversity sometimes you face  growing up that makes you into the  individual you are how do you give you  know your son who's obviously afforded  opportunities that you never had growing  up how do you give him that same kind of  those same experiences I don't think I'm  gonna have to give it to him I think the  world has a way of giving us struggles  even when you're born into a world where  you have a house and you have food and  you have a school and you have a father  who's gonna keep the world as safe as  possible for you the universe knows what  it has to do and he's gonna find his  struggles I don't have to give them to  him no one ever gave me my struggles I  found them myself  so I'm sure he'll find them I hope they  don't hurt too bad but I know that's  what's gonna make him grow and that's  his experience I'll pray for the  strength to accept whatever he has to go  through because I know it'll hurt me to  see him in pain of any kind  but you know maybe he's gonna be that  guy that just doesn't have to go through  quite as much hurt as his dad yeah which  would be awesome for ya yeah let him  have his hurts along the way but if it  doesn't have to be all the way down and  dirty that's fine  he's listening he's learning piano yeah  and he's a natural-born vocalist he  likes singing and we like writing songs  daily about anything and everything
 

